      A widespread belief among video editors is that importing an AI video into Adobe Premiere, Final Cut Pro, or CapCut and exporting it with a new codec will remove the watermark. In reality, standard video re-encoding does not eliminate SynthID:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Trimming and Splitting:</strong> Because the watermark pattern is present across every individual frame, selecting a short sub-clip leaves the full watermark structure intact in all exported frames.</li>
      <li><strong>H.264 / HEVC Re-compression:</strong> Motion estimation and discrete cosine transform quantization preserve the low-to-mid frequency bands where SynthID is embedded.</li>
      <li><strong>Frame Rate Conversion:</strong> Blending frames or converting 30 fps to 60 fps interpolates the watermark signal into the newly synthesized intermediate frames.</li>
    </ul>

